  "summary": "Four supplied candidates directly apply federated learning—expressed as decentralised training without pooled records—to hate-speech detection. [V0107] reports AUROC 0.94 on ProtMap; [V0105] reports accuracy 0.80 on ToxiBench; [V0108] reports F1 0.66 on FireScope; and [V0106] reports test MAE 0.87 on GridWatch. These results use different datasets and metrics and therefore are not directly comparable. No fifth supplied candidate satisfies both the method and topic requirements: [V0114] is included only as the nearest same-topic comparator, but it uses multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling rather than federated learning, reporting F1 0.74 on GridWatch.",
